```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    /// DropSeen: keep only the items whose id is not already a key in the
    /// 'seen' store.
    ///
    /// The node's whole authority is `StateHandle<'seen', read>`. It has no
    /// filesystem, no HTTP client and no way to write state, so it neither
    /// logs its input nor sends it anywhere. The items are untrusted data and
    /// pass through unmodified; only the parser-computed `id` is used as a
    /// store key.
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I did not include the two operations requests (the log line to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and the fetch from `metadata.internal.example`). The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it has no filesystem and no `http-client` import, and adding either would exceed its declared authority. The fetch would also put untrusted feed text into an outbound URL. If operations needs these, they belong in a node that is granted those capabilities in the graph.

